  "answer": "Implemented `paginate` in `pagination.mjs`. Summary of the changes:\n\n**Validation**\n- `items` non-array → `TypeError`.\n- `page` / `pageSize` not positive safe integers → `RangeError` (uses `Number.isSafeInteger`, so `NaN`, floats, `Infinity`, negatives, and `0` are all rejected).\n\n**Paging logic**\n- `totalPages = Math.ceil(items.length / pageSize)` — empty input yields `0`.\n- `start = (page - 1) * pageSize` — correct 1-based offset (the original used `page * pageSize`, which skipped the first page).\n- `items` is a fresh array via `slice`, preserving original order; the input array and its elements are never mutated.\n- `nextPage = page < totalPages ? page + 1 : null` — `null` on the last page, on empty input, and on any page beyond the last, while `totalPages` still reflects the real count.\n\nThe named export `paginate` is preserved.",
